The central lesson: Blockade warfare is not just naval warfare. It is the intersection of maritime power, international law, economic interdependence, geography, political coercion, and national resilience.

Understanding those connections is what separates someone who merely knows naval terminology from someone who understands blockade warfare as a field of strategic study.
